    'description' => '',
    'extract_html' => '<p><b><a href="/school1/ptable/element/Mg" class="wiki-link" title="Magnesium (Mg)"><a href="/school1/ptable/element/Mg" class="wiki-link" title="Magnesium (Mg)">Magnesium</a></a></b> (symbol <b>Mg</b>, atomic number 12) is a lightweight, silvery-white alkaline earth metal in Group 2 of the periodic table. Sharing a matching outer electron configuration with its five group siblings, it exhibits similar crystal structure and chemical reactivity. It is the ninth most abundant element in the universe, the eighth most abundant element in Earth\'s crust, and the second most abundant positive ion in seawater. Indispensable to life, <a href="/school1/ptable/element/Mg" class="wiki-link" title="Magnesium (Mg)">magnesium</a> rests at the heart of green chlorophyll molecules in plants to drive photosynthesis and serves as an essential spark for hundreds of metabolic enzymes in humans and animals.</p>',
