    'description' => '',
    'extract_html' => '<p><strong>Mendelevium</strong> is a synthetic, highly radioactive metal with the atomic number <strong>101</strong> and the symbol <strong>Md</strong>. Belonging to the actinide series, it is a transuranic element, which means it exists beyond uranium in the periodic table. Because it doesn\'t occur naturally on Earth, it must be created artificially in laboratories using particle accelerators. Mendelevium is renowned as a monumental achievement in nuclear chemistry, demonstrating that elements could be synthesized and identified even when produced literally one atom at a time.</p>',
    'local_image' => 'https://images-of-elements.com/s/mendelevium.jpg',
    'atomic_mass' => 258,
    'density' => NULL,
    'melt' => 1100,
    'boil' => NULL,
