    'description' => '',
    'extract_html' => '<p><strong>Tennessine (Ts)</strong> is a superheavy, synthetic element with the atomic number 117. It is one of the newest and heaviest elements on the periodic table, belonging to the halogen group (which includes fluorine and chlorine). However, because of its massive size and "relativistic effects," scientists predict it behaves more like a metal or metalloid than a typical halogen!</p>
<p>This elusive element cannot be found anywhere in nature. It is incredibly unstable and radioactive, surviving for only a tiny fraction of a second before decaying into lighter elements. Because it vanishes so quickly, scientists have only ever created a handful of tennessine atoms, making it a true marvel of modern nuclear physics.</p>',
