    'description' => '',
    'extract_html' => '<p><strong>Oganesson (symbol Og, atomic number 118)</strong> is a synthetic chemical element and the heaviest element currently known on the periodic table. Situated at the very bottom of Group 18, it is officially placed in the noble gas column. However, modern theoretical physics suggests it might behave more like a solid metal due to strange relativistic effects. It is highly radioactive and incredibly unstable, existing for only a tiny fraction of a second before decaying into lighter elements.</p>',
